  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation resolves H3 negatively for the claim of a clinically meaningful predictor association. H3 predicted EGFR-amplified lineages to have stronger EGFR dependency; because the hypothesis direction was -1, the signed estimates are positive when they support stronger dependency. Discovery R3 gave a signed effect of +0.0252, only about the absolute 10% threshold for dependency_EGFR (approximately 0.025 given the mean score magnitude of 0.25), and its 95% interval crossed zero. Independent validation R13 was weaker: signed +0.0152, below the 10% threshold, and its stricter validation interval also crossed zero. Taken together, the evidence does not support EGFR amplification as a clinically meaningful predictor of EGFR dependency in this dataset. I therefore reject H3 and close it as a negative finding, while acknowledging that intervals are wide enough that smaller or context-dependent effects are not definitively excluded. I also reject H7: the TP53-loss effect on MDM2 was signed +0.0088, far below the approximately 0.027 absolute threshold for dependency_MDM2, and its interval was compatible with no difference. In contrast, H13 should be accepted. The same strong evidence that rejected H10 supports the reversed association: KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, with a signed estimate of +0.796 and an extremely tight interval. Thus the original KEAP1-to-stronger-NFE2L2 hypothesis is rejected, but the opposite dataset association is accepted. The current dataset-supported associations are large and precise for SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, and KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. These are not causal claims. The next priority is specificity and within-dataset robustness. H14-H17 already registered POLR2A negative-control tests for KEAP1 loss, MSI-high, SMARCA4 loss, and TP53 loss; these are crucial because POLR2A is a broadly essential transcriptional machinery gene and should not be strongly associated with pathway-specific dependencies unless there is global screen-level confounding or a general bias. The new proposals H18-H21 test whether the accepted effects are stable across lung lineage_subtype adenocarcinoma versus non-adenocarcinoma subgroups. These subtype interactions do not retest whether the effects exist, but they ask whether the effects are concentrated in one histologic context or are internally robust across available lung subtypes. I will downgrade accepted associations if POLR2A negative controls are positive, and I will narrow interpretation of accepted associations if subtype interactions are large despite stable main effects. All conclusions remain limited to the supplied dataset, without causal or external generalizability claims.",
  "research_notes": "Synthesis update. H3 EGFR amplification EGFR dependency: rejected and closed after validation R13 failed to replicate a clinically meaningful effect; discovery R3 was borderline around threshold but validation estimate was below threshold and interval crossed zero. H7 TP53 loss MDM2 dependency: rejected and closed due to small effect far below clinical threshold and interval crossing zero. H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency: accepted from R10, reversing H10 as originally registered; very large and precise dataset association. Active accepted dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H8 TP53 loss weaker USP7 dependency; H9 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Negative and closed driver/population claims: H1 KRAS, H2 BRAF, H4 ERBB2, H6 ARID1A on SMARCA2, H10 original KEAP1 direction, H11 KRAS subtype interaction, H12 sex STAT3, plus H3 and H7 closed. Pending specificity controls: H14-H17 POLR2A tests for KEAP1, MSI, SMARCA4, TP53; if these show broad associations, accepted outcomes should be reconsidered as global screen associations rather than outcome-specific dependencies. New planned subtype interactions: H18-H21 test adenocarcinoma versus complement for accepted H5/H8/H9/H13 associations. Interpretations remain noncausal and dataset-specific."
}

