esult arises in a multiple-testing context. I therefore leave H22 unresolved and request independent validation. The remaining new comparisons H23-H25 are not clinically meaningful: BRCA2 loss/DHX9 estimate 0.012 against about 0.025 threshold, PIK3CA mutation/EGFR estimate -0.003 against about 0.025 threshold, and RB1 loss/KIF18A estimate 0.008 against about 0.026 threshold. All intervals include zero. I reject these as unsupported. Overall, the evidence supports the existing large dataset-specific associations but suggests no global POLR2A confounding, no meaningful adenocarcinoma subtype interaction, and no strong new associations except the unconfirmed MYC-USP7 candidate."
